WEBVTT

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:04.347
Scrap is easy to see. The reason it
keeps coming back is harder to find.

00:00:04.717 --> 00:00:07.896
Start with the losses you
already record: rejected parts,

00:00:07.896 --> 00:00:11.388
unplanned stops and time spent
getting a press back on setting.

00:00:12.098 --> 00:00:15.910
Vella Partners starts with two
questions. Which presses need attention?

00:00:15.910 --> 00:00:19.926
And when a defect appears on one of
them, what should the team check first?

00:00:20.636 --> 00:00:23.518
The field diagnostic starts
with the records you have,

00:00:23.518 --> 00:00:26.350
then checks them with the
people who run the presses.

00:00:26.720 --> 00:00:30.555
It separates measured losses from
estimates and missing information.

00:00:30.555 --> 00:00:34.178
The result is a short list of
presses and actions to prioritise.

00:00:34.888 --> 00:00:37.006
On a press that is not connected,

00:00:37.006 --> 00:00:40.153
the operator opens VP Expert
when a defect appears.

00:00:40.523 --> 00:00:44.107
The plastics and rubber libraries
use different checks for different

00:00:44.107 --> 00:00:48.470
processes. The operator selects the
defect and answers three short questions.

00:00:49.180 --> 00:00:53.235
The next screen shows a priority
check and explains why it was chosen.

00:00:53.235 --> 00:00:55.919
The operator records
what they actually find.

00:00:56.289 --> 00:00:58.330
A finding is not proof of a cause.

00:00:58.330 --> 00:01:01.338
An action has to be tested
and its outcome reviewed.

00:01:02.048 --> 00:01:06.370
The case links the defect, the checks,
the action and the observed result.

00:01:06.740 --> 00:01:10.281
A validated case can help the
next team facing the same problem.

00:01:10.281 --> 00:01:13.510
The demonstration is not a
library of real customer cases.

00:01:14.220 --> 00:01:18.101
On a connected press, VP Predict
compares successive measurements with a

00:01:18.101 --> 00:01:20.859
reference. A sustained
trend can trigger a warning

00:01:20.859 --> 00:01:23.515
even while the signal is
still within tolerance.

00:01:23.885 --> 00:01:27.736
The operator acknowledges it,
and VP Expert guides the checks.

00:01:28.446 --> 00:01:31.845
Start with the loss estimate,
investigate a visible defect,

00:01:31.845 --> 00:01:34.471
or replay a drift. These
are demonstrations,

00:01:34.471 --> 00:01:38.385
not approved machine instructions.
The decision stays with your team.
